 r←{parms}CloseProject projects;list;project;ind;res;buff;sources;inHash;performChecks;batch
⍝ Breaks the Link between a project and its folder on disk, and potentially executes a check functon afterwards.
⍝ In case ⍵ is empty, all projects in `#` are closed - but not any in `⎕SE`: opening one there is
⍝ unusual enough that whoever did it had a reason. Such a project is still closed when named.
⍝ `projects` may be one of:
⍝ 1. Empty vector (=close all)
⍝ 2. One or more project names like `#.Foo`
⍝ 3. One or more alias names like `[my-alias]`
⍝ 4. One or more paths of currently open projects
⍝ 5. A mixture of 2, 3 and 4
⍝ `parms` may be one or two integers, and a single one keeps its old meaning:
⍝ * [1] `performChecks` defaults to 1, meaning "perform checks, if any". A 0 prevents them.
⍝ * [2] `batch` defaults to 0. Set it to 1 when nobody is there to answer a question, so that a
⍝   `.linkconfig` carrying stops is left alone rather than asked about; see `HandleLinkSourceFlags`.\\
⍝ Returns the number of projects closed.
 r←0
 (performChecks batch)←{0<⎕NC ⍵:2↑(,⍎⍵),0 ⋄ 1 0}'parms'
 list←ListOpenProjects 1
 :If 0<≢list
⍝ Asked while the projects are still linked. `HandleLinkSourceFlags` needs the folder where Link keeps
⍝ its `.linkconfig`, and only Link knows it: this used to be handed `list[;2]`, the project HOME, and
⍝ further down even the namespace name, so `F.IsFile` was false either way and the global setting
⍝ `HandleLinkStops` never took effect on closing a project.
     sources←GetLinkSourceFolders list[;1]
     :If 0=≢projects
⍝ Projects in `#` only: opening one in `⎕SE` is unusual enough that whoever did it had a reason, and
⍝ "close all" must not interfere with it. Naming such a project explicitly still closes it.
         inHash←'#'=⊃¨list[;1]
         res←⎕SE.Link.Break¨inHash/list[;1]          ⍝ Only the first column names a namespace
         r←+/{'Unlinked: '{⍺≡(≢⍺)↑⍵}⍵}¨res
         {}batch HandleLinkSourceFlags¨{(0<≢¨⍵)/⍵}inHash/sources
     :Else
         list[;2]←F.NormalizePath list[;2]
         projects←,⊆projects
         :For project :In projects
             project←⍕project
             :If ∧/'[]'∊project
                 ind←list[;4]⍳⊂⎕C project~'[]'
             :Else
                 :If (∧/~'/\'∊project)∧~(1⊃project)∊'#⎕'
                     buff←(({⊃(-+/∧\~'⎕'=⊃¨⍵)↑⍵}⎕NSI),'.'),project
                     :If 9≠⊃⎕NC buff
                         :Continue
                     :EndIf
                     project←buff
                 :EndIf
                 ind←(⎕C list[;1])⍳⊂⎕C project
             :EndIf
             :If ind>≢list
                 ind←list[;2]⍳⊂F.NormalizePath project
             :EndIf
             :If ind≤≢list
                 res←⎕SE.Link.Break 1⊃list[ind;]
                 r+←'Unlinked: '{⍺≡(≢⍺)↑⍵}res
                 batch HandleLinkSourceFlags ind⊃sources
             :EndIf
         :EndFor
         :If performChecks
             ⍝ Right place for any checks...
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
